@startuml getOperationKeyAsync
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title
getOperationKeyAsync – Retrieve Operation Key
end title

participant "requestor" as requestor
participant "Operation Server Interface" as osi #LightCyan
participant "JSON Driver" as jd #LightYellow
participant "config.json" as cfg #LightGrey

note over requestor
  - operationServerUuid
end note

requestor -> osi: (operationServerUuid)
activate osi

osi -> jd: read logical-termination-point
activate jd

jd <-> cfg: retrieve control-construct

jd --> osi: Operation Server List from LTP 
deactivate jd

note over osi
  <u>Processing</u>
  - Locate operation-server LTP with matching UUID  
  - Read operation-server-interface configuration  
  - Extract operation-key attribute  
  - Return operationKey if found  
  - Return undefined if not present
end note

osi --> requestor: operationKey | undefined
deactivate osi

@enduml
